description: gate.sh prints each row's wall time and records it, so we can see which checks cost the most before deciding what to make cheaper.
 
 Facts that close it:
 
 - F1 every ok and FAIL line carries the row's wall seconds: gate.sh's self-test through LW_GATE_ROWS (command and output).
 - F2 each run appends one line per row to a timings ledger with the revision, the load average and the slots held when it started (a file:line of the format, and a sample).
 - F3 everything that reads gate output still reads it: a search for its consumers, and their rows pass (command and exit).
